---
title: History
order: 4
description: Log, diff, show, blame, bisect, and shortlog
tags: [git, log, diff, show, blame, bisect, shortlog, history]
---

Inspecting repository history and changes between commits.

@code bash
# Basic log
git log
git log --oneline                # compact: hash + message
git log --oneline -10            # last 10 commits
git log --graph --oneline --all  # ASCII branch graph
git log --stat                   # show changed files per commit
git log -p                       # show full patches
git log --format="%h %an %s"    # custom format

# Filter log
git log --author="name"
git log --since="2 weeks ago"
git log --until="2025-01-01"
git log --grep="fix"             # search commit messages
git log -S "functionName"        # commits that add/remove string (pickaxe)
git log -G "regex"               # commits matching regex in diff
git log -- path/to/file          # commits touching specific file
git log main..feature            # commits in feature not in main
git log main...feature           # commits in either but not both

@text
Diff shows changes between commits, staging area, and working tree.

@code bash
# Working tree vs staging area
git diff
git diff file.go                 # single file

# Staging area vs last commit
git diff --staged
git diff --cached                # same as --staged

# Between commits/branches
git diff main feature-auth
git diff HEAD~3 HEAD
git diff abc1234 def5678
git diff main...feature          # changes since branches diverged

# Diff options
git diff --stat                  # summary only
git diff --name-only             # just filenames
git diff --name-status           # filenames with status (A/M/D)
git diff --word-diff             # inline word-level diff
git diff --color-words           # colored word diff
git diff -w                      # ignore whitespace changes

@text
Show displays a commit's metadata and diff. Blame annotates each line
with the commit that last modified it.

@code bash
# Show commit details
git show HEAD
git show abc1234
git show HEAD:path/to/file       # show file at specific commit
git show v1.0                    # show tag details
git show --stat HEAD             # summary only

# Blame: who changed each line
git blame file.go
git blame -L 10,20 file.go      # lines 10-20 only
git blame -L :funcName file.go  # lines of a function
git blame -w                     # ignore whitespace
git blame -C                     # detect code moved from other files
git blame --since="3 months ago" file.go

@text
Bisect performs binary search to find the commit that introduced a bug.

@code bash
# Manual bisect
git bisect start
git bisect bad                   # current commit is bad
git bisect good v1.0             # v1.0 was good
# Git checks out a middle commit. Test it, then:
git bisect good                  # or: git bisect bad
# Repeat until the first bad commit is found
git bisect reset                 # return to original branch

# Automated bisect with a test script
git bisect start HEAD v1.0
git bisect run make test         # script exits 0=good, 1-124/126-127=bad

# Show bisect log
git bisect log

@text
Shortlog summarizes git log output by author.

@code bash
# Commits per author
git shortlog -sn                 # sorted by count
git shortlog -sne                # include email
git shortlog --since="1 month ago"
git shortlog main..feature       # for a branch
